  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="summary">
        <p>Known as Greenhill House in 1893 when my great-great-grandmother Emma Haines died there at home with daughter Janie Haddow and son-in-law Jim.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="detail">
        <p>Jim and Janie had married in Hobart in 1884. Janie's parents had moved to Melbourne from Sandy Bay in 1888.</p>
        <p>Jim was one of the sons of Andrew Haddow of 'Haddow and Sons' hardware store of North Melbourne. Haddow's Lane near the corner of Queensbury and Errol St commemorates the family's association with the district.</p>
        <p>Emma, Janie and Jim were interred at the Carlton General Cemetery.</p>
      </div>
    </body>
